
== 1 — drawing twenty rows costs twenty rows, not ten thousand ==
rows in the source: 10000
cell reads under a hundred: true
cell reads over zero: true

== 2 — a second frame with nothing changed reads nothing ==
reads after an idle frame: 0

== 3 — scrolling by less than a row reads nothing new ==
offset moved to 4
reads after a four-point scroll: 0

== 4 — scrolling a whole page reads about a page ==
offset after scrolling down 600: 604
reads after a 600-point scroll are under two hundred: true
and over zero: true

== 4b — and scrolling back up is the other sign ==
offset after scrolling back: 4

== 5 — one editor at a time ==
editing row 0 column 1
after a second edit: row 3 column 1

== 6 — Return commits and Escape cancels ==
committed: row 5 column 1: Espresso
the source kept it: Espresso
editor after commit: row -1
editor after cancel: row -1
row six is unchanged: Cup 0

== 7 — a column the policy refuses cannot be edited ==
column 0 editable: false
column 1 editable: true
